From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 09:25:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] linux 3.10: disable blanket -Werror for arch/mips

This vendor kernel is built with a modern GCC 14 toolchain. The MIPS tree
unconditionally adds `-Werror`, which turns numerous compatibility warnings
in legacy code paths into hard failures even after the correct T31/XBurst
machine configuration is selected.

Drop the blanket `-Werror` and let real compile errors fail the build while
non-fatal warnings remain visible.
---
 arch/mips/Kbuild | 4 +---
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/Kbuild b/arch/mips/Kbuild
index 68eab20..a48d51b 100644
--- a/arch/mips/Kbuild
+++ b/arch/mips/Kbuild
@@ -1,7 +1,5 @@
-# Fail on warnings - also for files referenced in subdirs
-# -Werror can be disabled for specific files using:
-# CFLAGS_<file.o> := -Wno-error
-subdir-ccflags-y := -Werror
+# Legacy vendor MIPS code emits warnings with modern GCC; keep them visible
+# without promoting them to hard failures.
 
 # platform specific definitions
 include arch/mips/Kbuild.platforms
-- 
2.47.0
